<body>
<abstractGroup>
<abstract>
<p>We present wind tunnel results for a <italic>shape-memory alloy</italic> actuated morphing wing that achieves continuous camber variation from 2% to 8% chord.</p>
</abstract>
</abstractGroup>
<section>
<title>Experimental Setup</title>
<p>Tests were conducted in the 2.4 m × 1.8 m closed-circuit wind tunnel at Reynolds numbers from 2×10^5 to 8×10^5.</p>
<figure>
<label>Figure 1</label>
<caption><p>Schematic of the morphing wing test section with SMA actuator locations</p></caption>
</figure>
</section>
<section>
<title>Results</title>
<p>Lift coefficient C_L increased by <bold>34%</bold> at α = 5° when camber was morphed from 2% to 8%.</p>
